    fix(fleet-ops): deploy-doc arm grades the deploy path, not a filename spelling (SCHED-GAP-16989)
    
    The census's deploy-doc check matched seven exact filenames. The fleet's real
    convention is `deploy/README.md` beside a unit directory, or
    `docs/runbook-<topic>.md`, or `INSTALL.md`. `exists_ci` matches whole basenames,
    so none of those can ever equal `docs/runbook.md` — and 35 of 88 families were
    reported as having a tribal deploy path while shipping a fully documented one.
    Nothing a project lane could action, so the class re-reported on every 24h ops
    tick and buried the findings that were real.
    
    Stage 4 of the chain: a deploy-path doc is recognised by a basename hint
    (deploy|runbook|operations|install|setup|provision) with a doc extension, or by
    sitting in a deploy directory (`deploy/README.md`), depth-limited to the root and
    its two nearest levels with build output and harness bookkeeping pruned. The
    seven canonical spellings still pass first, so nothing that passed can start
    failing.
    
    Measured, not asserted:
    
      arms   patches/fleet-ops-deploy-doc.test.py   7/7 after, 4/7 before
             the three that fail before are the defect (deploy/README.md,
             docs/runbook-<topic>.md, INSTALL.md); the four guard arms hold on both
             modules, so the fix cannot trade a false positive for a false negative
             (no deploy artifact still reports; a doc buried in vendor/ or dist/
             still reports)
      fleet  deploy-doc 35 -> 4 families, and no family gained any check
      family coding-hermes-scheduler (the family that triggered the check):
             deploy-doc GONE, its container gap still reports
      surv.  the 4 survivors verified by hand as genuine gaps
      gate   scripts/verify-patch.sh PASS — 5 stages, 4 patches, live digest
